codex
The new evidence explains why the wrong-path instruction retires: the redirect flush loses priority to `any_stall` in the IF/EX register. In the failing cases the younger fall-through instruction is a mul/div or otherwise stalls, so `pc_redirect` arrives but IF/EX holds the wrong-path instruction instead of flushing it. This is a real DUT bug; I’m fixing redirect priority over ordinary stalls while preserving `mem_stall` freeze.
