codex
The remaining first mismatches are again after taken branches, but now immediately at the next branch target: for example seed 2026061201 matches through `bgeu gp,sp,0x106` at PC `0xf8`, then the DUT falls through to `0xfc` while Spike jumps to `0x106`. I’m checking branch operand values from the matched commit stream to see whether this is operand/compare logic rather than flush timing.
