Internal debug shows the first branch at `0xec` resolves taken and redirects correctly. The next committed “branch” at `0xf8` does not appear as `id_is_branch` internally, which means the core is retiring PC `0xf8` with a different decoded instruction than the memory/disassembly at that PC. I’m adding a narrow PC debug to capture the actual IF/EX instruction at `0xf8`.
apply patch
